As far as memory serves; in my early Nethack days I seem to have died
often from magic trap effects, much more often than now. And, frankly,
I am not quite sure what exactly I am doing different nowadays. But I
think that the main difference is that now I don't try to kill those
monsters, but, by hitting at a single foe, try to open a breach that
will provide a good escape path; then I flee as soon as possible. In
case I have a scroll of teleport - you know that you can read scrolls
even blind! -, and if I am too weak to survive a couple turns, I will
pronounce the formula on it to immediately escape, or if I have a wand
of digging, I dig down through the floor. From a very early trap you
will usually get only comparably weak monsters, so the breach attempt
might work. Mind also that the Mines have wide areas, and often lacking
close and sufficiently narrow alleys to retreat; so it might be better
to examine the main dungeon branch first until you are buff enough to
do the mines.

